module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_store_root_nothing_creates

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread, BlockerClassUnstated }

data a_store_root_nothing_creates: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_store_root_nothing_creates" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**a durable slot store is read under a root that no deployment route creates** (the CAS slot store, gunbc.durable_cas_file_store, refuses a root it cannot list rather than reading it as an empty slot, so the first read of a never-created root stops its consumer: absence is not established, and the refusal is correct).",

    "INVALID STATE: a store module declares the path of its root and reads and writes under it, while the one list both deployment routes ensure and read back (gunbc.roadmap.dashboard_instance_directories dashboard_instance_directory_demands) carries no row for it and no other capability creates it.",

    "HARM, TWO INSTANCES. 2026-10-16: the srv1 lab's first claude dispatch stopped at its credential snapshot, 'the directory .../credential-acquisition-slots could not be listed' (repaired by gunbc.dispatch_credential_acquisition credential_acquisition_slots_directory). 2026-10-20: the lab's first dispatch past #14235 stopped at the spawn step worktree-claim for EVERY executor, 'the directory <instance>/attempt-state/worktree-claims could not be listed', and the session placement was released; production serves a build that predates #14235, so its first deploy past it would have stopped every dispatch at the same step (repaired by gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim_root worktree_claim_slots_directory).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the refusal is fail-closed and located, so nothing runs wrong; the cost is a whole dispatch factory stopped by a directory. The store's own witnesses are green because they write under a root the test creates; only a deploy that omits the row shows it. There were two creators in the corpus for one class (the instance directory list, and belt_session_slots_ensure for the session slot store); the belt ensure was deleted when the session slot store took its own declared row (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_attempt_slots_root session_attempt_slots_directory), so the list is the one creator. Compute seat directories are the declared exception: one per dispatch attempt, created by the provider from their declared target (gunbc.compute.compute_attempt_slots_root compute_seat_directory) under the listed compute root.",

    "RUNG: found at 1 (a live dispatch refused), twice. Now 2 for the three stores the join enumerates: a root with no row in the list goes red in a witness, but the witness enumerates its stores by authorship, so a third store nobody lists is still writable. CEILING 3, next trigger D14 step 4 (docs/plans/ensure-closure-design.md section 12), which derives the demand from the code that writes, at which point the join is not authored and the class has no constructor. The witness evaluates only in a witness run; the required job evaluates none (gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn).",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a new durable slot store declares its root's creator in the same change, as a row in the instance directory list, and the join test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance_witness every_slot_store_root_has_a_declared_creator names it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
